Reproducing the S2R Lean proof
==============================

This directory is a Lake project. lean-toolchain selects Lean 4.19.0;
lakefile.toml requires Mathlib v4.19.0; lake-manifest.json pins all resolved
dependency revisions. The Lean development is in S2R/. S2R.lean imports
S2R.All, so the default lake build includes the current main result.

The paper is ../paper.tex, with citations in ../references.bib. The theorem
scope, proof-module map, audit assumptions and resource-model boundaries are
documented in FORMALIZATION_STATUS in this directory.

Directory roles
---------------
S2R/                 Definitions, algorithm, proofs and resource bounds
S2R.lean             Lake library root importing S2R.All
verify_s2r.py        Complete rebuild, theorem and axiom audit
lakefile.toml        Mathlib dependency declaration
lake-manifest.json   Locked dependency revisions
lean-toolchain       Lean compiler version
.lake/               Downloaded dependencies and compiled modules (ignored)
audit/               Generated report and logs (ignored)

Main result
-----------
S2R.Instance.s2r_verified_streaming returns an owned feasible selection
whose value equals the S2R output and satisfies the exact 1-1/e guarantee.
For n>=1 it also proves Q<=n^3 value queries, A<=141*n^3 charged auxiliary
operations and P<=66*n^2 peak abstract RAM words. The full polynomial bounds
also cover n=0; see FORMALIZATION_STATUS and paper.tex.

The resource model is exact-real unit-cost RAM, with explicit client arrays
and register cells. It excludes oracle-private memory, serialization,
numerical bit complexity and Lean evaluator or machine-code runtime/heap.

Build and audit from a clean clone
----------------------------------
Install Git, Python 3 and elan (which provides lake and installs the Lean
version selected by lean-toolchain). The first dependency/cache fetch needs
network access. From the repository root run:

  cd verification
  lake exe cache get
  lake build
  python -B verify_s2r.py

The script rebuilds S2R modules through lake env lean, checks the required
main declarations, rejects forbidden proof placeholders, prints axiom
dependencies for every named theorem and rechecks imports with --trust=0.
It writes audit/verification_report.json and per-module logs. Exit code 0
with status COMPLETE means all required main results passed; exit code 1
means a build or audit failure; exit code 2 means checked components passed
but the main result is missing. The report records source hashes for that run.
The generated audit directory is ignored by Git. GitHub Actions performs the
same checks on a clean checkout and uploads the report as a CI artifact.

For an offline local check with an existing compiled Mathlib installation,
S2R_LEAN may point to a Lean executable and LEAN_PATH to the required compiled
library directories. The report then records compiler_invocation: direct Lean.
This local mode still checks all S2R modules and axioms, but the clean-clone
Lake build above remains the publication check for dependency reproducibility.

Key source paths
----------------
Basic.lean, Algorithm.lean, Main.lean: instance assumptions, candidates and
the exact approximation theorem.
Residual.lean, PathBounds.lean, DynamicCertificate.lean,
EntropyConnection.lean, SmallDomain.lean, NormalizedContradiction.lean:
path estimates, analytic certificates and the normalized contradiction.
Compression.lean, RepairImplementation.lean, RuntimeRefinement.lean,
ThinComplexity.lean: candidate equivalence and query/operation bounds.
StreamingRows.lean, OwnedOutput.lean, StreamingComplexity.lean: streamed
evaluation, owned output and the joint resource theorem.
All.lean: one import entry for the current development.
